latest_plan = "Based on the reflection and insights gained, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Initialize:\n   - Create a copy of the input grid to work on.\n   - Create a set to keep track of processed cells.\n\n2. Identify Seed Patterns:\n   - Scan the edges of the grid (top, bottom, left, right).\n   - For each non-black cell on an edge, identify the continuous line it's part of.\n   - Store these lines as seed patterns, noting their orientation (horizontal or vertical) and position.\n\n3. Process Seed Patterns:\n   - For each seed pattern:\n     a. Determine Expansion Direction:\n        - If horizontal, try to expand vertically.\n        - If vertical, try to expand horizontally.\n     \n     b. Find Expansion Limits:\n        - Scan in the expansion direction until a non-black cell or grid boundary is reached.\n        - This defines the rectangle for potential filling.\n     \n     c. Check for Alternating Patterns:\n        - If expanding vertically, check for other horizontal patterns within the expansion rectangle.\n        - If multiple patterns exist, prepare to alternate them.\n     \n     d. Fill the Rectangle:\n        - If expanding horizontally, repeat the vertical seed pattern across the width.\n        - If expanding vertically:\n          - If single pattern, repeat it down the height.\n          - If multiple patterns, alternate them down the height.\n     \n     e. Mark Processed:\n        - Add all filled cells to the processed set.\n\n4. Identify New Seed Patterns:\n   - Scan the edges of the newly filled rectangles.\n   - Any non-black cells that aren't in the processed set become new seed patterns.\n\n5. Repeat:\n   - Go back to step 3 with the new seed patterns.\n   - Continue this process until no new seed patterns are found.\n\n6. Final Check:\n   - Scan the entire grid for any remaining unfilled (black) cells that are adjacent to filled cells.\n   - If found, use the adjacent filled cell's color to fill it, extending the pattern logically.\n\n7. Return Result:\n   - Once no more changes can be made, return the transformed grid.\n\nImplementation Notes:\n- Use efficient data structures like sets for tracking processed cells and queues for managing seed patterns.\n- Implement helper functions for common operations like finding continuous lines, determining expansion limits, and filling rectangles.\n- When alternating patterns vertically, cycle through the available patterns in order.\n- Always prioritize longer patterns over shorter ones when multiple options are available.\n- Ensure that the expansion process respects existing filled areas and doesn't overwrite them.\n\nThis plan should be able to handle all the cases presented in the challenge, including complex scenarios with multiple interacting patterns and regions. It captures the core ideas of rectangular expansion, pattern alternation, and iterative processing that seem to be central to the puzzle's logic."
